      "root_cause_candidate": "The drm/xe driver's `exec` and `vm_bind` ioctls lacked bounds checking on the `num_syncs` field, allowing userspace to supply an arbitrary value that caused excessive kernel memory allocations.",
      "evidence_points": "The CVE description states \"Without bounds checking, a very large num_syncs can force an excessively large allocation,\" and the patch adds validation logic `args->num_syncs > DRM_XE_MAX_SYNCS` in `xe_exec.c` and `xe_vm.c` to reject values exceeding the defined limit."
